 <h2>Important limits - read before importing</h2><ul><li><strong>A real Shopify import has never been tested.</strong> Column names follow the official help page (<a href="https://help.shopify.com/en/manual/products/import-export/using-csv">help.shopify.com/en/manual/products/import-export/using-csv</a>); <code>Option2 name</code> is inferred from the documented pattern. Compare with the sample CSV from your own admin first.</li><li><code>Status</code> and <code>Published on online store</code> are not emitted. Per the docs, omitted values default to active/published, so imported products may go live immediately.</li><li>Importing over existing handles can overwrite existing products. Try a few products in a development or test store first.</li><li>Native CSV gives each variant ONE variant image. Showing 5 pictures only for the selected color is a theme or app feature, not something this CSV establishes.</li><li>Images must already be at public URLs. No inventory, weight, SEO, metafield or market columns.</li></ul>
